# Render reads its build and start commands from render.yaml at the repo
# root, not from this file — render.yaml's `startCommand` is what actually
# launches the service. This Procfile is kept only as a fallback for running
# the app on a Procfile-driven host (or a Render service created without a
# blueprint), and must be kept in step with render.yaml's startCommand.
#
# A `release:` line previously lived here declaring the migration step. That
# was Heroku syntax: Render ignores it, so migrations were in fact only ever
# run by render.yaml's buildCommand. It has been removed rather than fixed,
# so there is exactly one place that defines how migrations run.
web: gunicorn config.wsgi --log-file -
